  "RESOLVED
1. kotoba-lang/shell window host now compiles (root cause: `5c39631` added call sites without declarations) — `658dfde`.
2. `--web-url` now mounts a WKWebView, and the runtime forwards it — `658dfde`.
3. `apps/tamaki-observer-web` focus ring now points at `--color-primitive-yellow-300` — `658dfde`. Source only; `dist/style.css` is regenerated by the shadow `:compile-finish` hook, and was left alone because another session had it open.
4. The native chat button posted an empty prompt on every click (`perform` never emitted the `.value` its consumer reads) — `658dfde`.

OPEN
5. cloud-itonami-app: the Worker UI is verified structurally, over HTTP, and as a native WKWebView render of the live app with its real script running and zero JS errors. It has NOT been driven through a completed passkey ceremony, because that needs a real authenticator. Closing this needs a WebAuthn virtual authenticator in the host, not more test coverage.
6. Workspace: `nbb scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs --check` reports STALE on plain `origin/main`, independent of any single entry — whole-fleet local-checkout drift, because the generator pins from local working HEADs. Deliberately not addressed: the only way to make it green is the wholesale regeneration that is forbidden. The `--check` signal is therefore not usable as a gate in its current form.
7. Workspace: `manifest/docs-edn-only.cljs verify` fails on **33 pre-existing files** — 22 with genuine EDN syntax corruption (unmatched delimiters, duplicate map keys, odd-form maps, invalid tokens like `off:` and `80+`), 7 ADRs that parse but are not tx-data, 4 path-md-refs. Concentrated in `90-docs/deployment/MONTH-3-*` and `90-docs/gates/*`. Unrelated to this ADR and not fixed here: repairing them means reconstructing intent in documents this work does not own. Worth its own pass.
8. Environment: an orphaned process (`resource-guard run build -- clojure -M:server`, PPID 1) holds the workspace-wide `build` scope lock, so a long-running server blocks every session's builds. Left alone — not this session's process. The underlying flaw is that a server was started under the `build` scope at all.
9. cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-app: the shared west checkout is stuck behind `origin/main` because another session holds uncommitted edits to `web.clj`, `server.clj`, `identity.clj`, `deps.edn` and `core_test.clj` there. Their edits are based on a pre-token-fix tree, so committing them may revert the token fix and worker routes. This is the shared-checkout-direct-edit hazard, and it can only be resolved by that session."
